Theorem 1.1 asserts that FK has a unique global minimizer qu if and only if K ≤1. In particular,
if K > 1, then we have nonuniqueness of critical points of FK. On the other hand, if K ≤1/2, the
theorem asserts that qu is the unique critical point of FK. Thus, there remains a gap K ∈(1/2, 1) in
which we have uniqueness of the global minimizer but do not know whether we also have uniqueness
of critical points. This gap reflects a limitation of our method (see the discussion of the proof below),
and it would be interesting to determine whether uniqueness of critical points holds for all K ≤1,
which we tentatively conjecture to be the case.
