C. Ablation Study
We conduct two ablation studies to analyze the contributions
of the key SAGR components.
The first ablation study evaluates how different contextual
information provided to the LLM affects coordination per-
formance. In the full SAGR framework, the LLM receives
structured information including room connectivity, frontier
statistics, task specification, and a brief plan summary de-
scribing the intended coordination strategy. To evaluate their
importance, we remove each component individually and
measure the resulting search performance.
Table III reports the average completion time for the se-
mantic search task. Removing any component consistently
