2
Angular twist deformation of Minkowski space
The Drinfel’d twist formalism allows for various noncommutative deformations of Minkowski space
and enables the construction of field theories thereon.
Noncommutativity breaks the standard
Poincar´e symmetry and replaces it with a twisted Poincar´e symmetry. Twisted Poincar´e symmetry
for field theories with the canonical Moyal deformation was introduced in [25,26], and elaborated in
detail in [27]. The κ-Minkowski space, originally introduced in [28] as a module over the κ-deformed
Poincar´e algebra, can also be realised as a twist deformation. U(1) gauge theory on κ-Minkowski
space is studied in [29], while certain cosmological implications have been explored via a Jordanian
twist formalism in [30,31].
The ρ- and λ-Minkowski spaces, which appear as members of a family with twisted Poincar´e
symmetries including κ-Minkowski space [32], arise from an angular twist deformation [10]; quan-
tum field theory and quantum mechanics on these spaces are discussed in [11–13, 33, 34]. In this
section we briefly review the deformation leading to the λ-Minkowski space, and then present a
novel framework for studying scalar field theories thereon in terms of cylindrical harmonics.
2.1
