⋆-theory
The homotopy algebra underlying the noncommutative cubic scalar field theory defined by (2.7)
is most straightforwardly constructed by applying the Drinfel’d twist deformation formalism, with
the angular twist operator (2.3), directly to the L∞-algebra which organises the corresponding
commutative theory; the latter is in fact a differential graded Lie algebra (in the category of L∞-
algebras). In this way we obtain the braided L∞-algebra which completely determines the classical
Φ3
⋆-theory (in the category of braided L∞-algebras). From this perspective, it is more natural to
start with the quantization of Φ3
⋆-theory as a braided quantum field theory. In this section we give
an elaborate account of this.
