analyst. When a man i and a woman j marry, their match generates a surplus ˜Φij
which they can share freely. Singles match to “0”: a single man i attains a utility of
˜Φi0 and a single woman j attains ˜Φ0j.
This paper will assume that the sets of types are finite: X “ t1, . . . , Xu and
Y “ t1, . . . , Y u.
As mentioned in the introduction, Dupuy and Galichon (2014)
extend the model to continuous types. We will denote by ˜Φ “ p˜Φijqi“1,...,I;j“1,...,J the
matrix of surpluses.
A matching is a list of numbers pµij, µi0, µ0jqi“1,...,I;j“1,...,J, with µij “ 1 if i and j
