1.1.2
Inference
Now suppose that the distributions of the unobserved heterogeneity terms (resp. the
joint surplus matrix Φ) are known up to a parameter vector α (resp. β), and that the
model is identified from data on a single market3. For any value of α, the generalized
entropy Eα can be evaluated easily—often in closed form. Given observed matching
