The stable matching µ is homogeneous of degree 1 in the vector pn, mq: if the
numbers of men and women of each type are multiplied by a common positive integer
k, then all numbers of marriages µxy and of singles µx0 and µ0y are multiplied by k
as well. On the other hand, utilities are unchanged; in that sense, there is no scale
effect in a separable matching market.
As the matching patterns maximize the social welfare, which is globally convex, its
Hessian must be semi-definite positive at the optimum. This entails testable impli-
cations that (depending on the available data) may allow for tests of the separability
assumption (see Galichon and Salani´e 2022).
