aggregation sum, total row value, comparison argmax, comparison argmax
rows, and kth row value), while M3-14B is strongest on retrieval (lookup by
header=99.2%, lookup list by header=88.3%).
In this oracle setting, retrieval categories approach saturation for the strongest
models (e.g., lookup by header reaches 99.2% with M3-14B). Nevertheless, nu-
merical reasoning remains substantially harder: the best accuracy for consistency
diff total is 55.1% (Q3-32B), indicating that multi-step arithmetic and con-
straint adherence remain a major source of errors even when perception is
removed. Overall, Q3-32B achieves the best oracle-HTML accuracy (83.4%),
closely followed by Q3-30B (82.6%).
