As already stated, we consider viscoelastic systems, such as RVEs, meta-
materials or structures, that can be evaluated exactly, i. e., whose generalized
stress histories σt(τ) can be evaluated for every generalized strain history
ϵt(τ), albeit at considerable computational expense. For instance, ϵt(τ) and
σt(τ) may refer to the average strain and stress of an RVE. However, an
explicit analytical representation of the corresponding hereditary law is not
