5. Numerical tests
In this section, we present two numerical examples that illustrate the ap-
proximation properties of the optimal history representation presented in
the foregoing: i) a simple one-dimensional standard linear solid; and ii) a
representative volume element (RVE) in the form of a regular polycrystal,
intended to exemplify how the method of approximation applies to situ-
ations where the material behavior is characterized by way of multiscale
analysis. It bears emphasis that similar procedures apply mutatis mutandi
when material behavior is characterized experimentally.
