the symmetric spin product Si ·Sj. Generally, the mech-
anism by which electric polarization arises from the spin
configuration via this inner-product form, thereby cou-
pling the spin system to the electric field, is known as
exchange striction. In Appendix A, we derive this form
of the coupling term starting from a concrete electronic
model.
Also, it should be noted that magnetoelectric
coupling, in which the electric polarization is propor-
tional to the spin vector product, has also been estab-
lished based on microscopic electroic mechanisms [43, 44].
