II. BACKGROUND
A. Preliminaries
We will briefly recollect and set notation for the theory of harmonic analysis of compact Lie groups and symmetric spaces,
which can be viewed in more detail in classical references such as [21], [6], [22] or [11], [13] for a more probabilistic approach.
For the compact and connected Lie group G we denote by λ its normalized probability Haar measure λ(G) = 1. The collection
of equivalence classes of irreducible linear representations of G, identified up to isomorphism, is denoted by bG. By standard
procedure of mixing by λ, each class in bG contains a unitary representation (π, Vπ) for Vπ a linear space of finite dimension
dπ and π : G →U(Vπ), where U(Vπ) is the group of unitary invertible linear endomorphisms of Vπ. With abuse of language,
we will always choose a unitary representation to represent each class in bG and without further care use notation such as
π ∈bG for such a unitary representation π. Recall in particular that bG is countable, that all irreducible representations of G
are finite-dimensional, and that each π ∈bG is countably infinitely differentiable π ∈C∞(G).
