Definition 5.6. A weak B–ring is a 6–tuple (X, ∨, 0, ·, 1,ˆ), where X is a set, ∨
and · are binary operations on X, 0, 1 ∈X and ˆ is a unary operation on X ( ˆx ∈X).
These obey the following axioms.
(X, ∨, 0) is a commutative monoid:
(1) (x ∨y) ∨z = x ∨(y ∨z)
