(X, ·, 1) is a monoid:
(4) (x · y) · z = x · (y · z)
∀x, y, z ∈X;
(5) x · 1 = x = 1 · x
∀x ∈X.
0 is an absorbing element:
(6) x · 0 = 0 = 0 · x
∀x ∈X.
The second operation is distributive with regard to the first operation:
(7) x · (y ∨z) = (x · y) ∨(x · z)
∀x, y, z ∈X;
(8) (x ∨y) · z = (x · z) ∨(y · z)
∀x, y, z ∈X.
The unary operation has some basic properties:
(9) ˆˆx = x
∀x ∈X;
(10) x ∨ˆx = ˆx ∨x
∀x ∈X;
(11) x · ˆx = ˆx · x
∀x ∈X.
