5. Symbol Length
The symbol length of an element ω ∈Kn(F)/2mKnF is the minimal number of symbols in
Kn(F)/2mKnF required to express it. In this section we study what bounds on the symbol length
of ω if we know its symbol length in Kn(F)/2m+1Kn(F).
Theorem 5.1. Consider a class ω ∈K2(F)/2mK2(F).
(a) If its symbol length in K2(F)/2m+1K2(F) is 2, then its symbol length in K2(F)/2mK2(F) is at
most 5.
(b) If its symbol length in K2(F)/2m+1K2(F) is 3, then its symbol length in K2(F)/2mK2(F) is at
most 15.
(c) If its symbol length in K2(F)/2m+1K2(F) is 4, then its symbol length in K2(F)/2mK2(F) is at
most 40.
