correspondence [54–56] with direct connection to entanglement theory [57–64]. Here
the tensors (13) are the natural objects, and they identify the SLOCC classes of
three-qubit entanglement [34] (see in Table 1) in parallel to the FTS-rank, identified
by the tensors (13) [46]. Note also that, although ga is not an entanglement mea-
sure [17, 44, 47], it is still relevant as an indicator function used in the entanglement
theory of mixed three-qubit states [44, 47].
