Corollary 3.17 (2ℵ1 = ℵ2). M(S, L) is strongly S-proper, strongly L-proper
and has the ℵ3-Knaster condition. Hence, it preserves all cardinals. More-
over, M(S, L) preserves 2ℵ1 = ℵ2.
The forcing M(S, L) adds a two-type symmetric system that covers H(κ)V
and an ω1-club subset of ω2 that avoids all infinite subsets from the ground
model. Moreover, in [7], it was also proven that M(S, L) adds a Kurepa
tree on ω2. Variants of the same forcing add a club subset of ω2, a function
on ω2 that bounds every canonical function below ω3 on a club, and a
simplified (ω2, 1)-morass. Furthermore, these variants of M(S, L) retain the
preservation properties given by Corollary 3.17.
