6.2
Will In-context Learning improve the performance of DP reasoning?
Previous work has shown that in-context learning, especially few-shot chain-of-thought prompting, can substantially
improve model performance on mathematical reasoning tasks (Wei et al., 2022). We focus on the Private Selection with
Laplace Noise task in Category 1 LaplaceRNM, which is challenging for most LLMs, with most models achieving
relatively low accuracy (Table 2). Because instances in this task family are relatively homogeneous and admit similar
proof structures, in-context learning is particularly natural in this setting. We therefore conduct a one-shot experiment
with GPT-5-minimal using a single question–answer exemplar for the Laplace Report Noisy Max mechanism. The
proof template (Appendix C.4.2) is adapted from Theorem A.8. Under this one-shot prompt, both models we tested
have improved performance, as shown in Table 5.
