On a miss, the adversary must reconstruct block A[vj] by
replaying its write chain: the block was overwritten ρ times
in expectation, each overwrite requiring one hash for the data
field and one for the causal field, plus the final read itself,
totaling 2ρ+1 hash evaluations per miss. (The 2× factor from
causal hashes is the constant described in §II-H, Role 3.)
