Why ρ ≥4. At ρ = 4 and α = 0 (no storage), the TMTO
penalty is Tadv/Thonest = 1+(2·4+1) = 10×. This exceeds the
measured ASIC advantage (∼2×) by 5×: a storage-reducing
adversary is strictly worse off than one with faster hardware.
Verification cost is independent of ρ (it depends on Q, d, R,
