1
Introduction
1.1
Why MPECs are difficult
A mathematical program with equilibrium constraints (MPEC) is an optimization problem in which
some constraints are themselves equilibrium conditions. Canonical examples include complementarity
systems, variational inequalities, and KKT systems of lower-level optimization problems.
A basic abstract form is
