which yields the lowest overall performance. Constrained
by the memoryless nature of standard VLA models, this
baseline is incapable of implicitly tracking task progress. For
instance, given largely identical inputs, repetitive grasping
and releasing actions frequently occur, causing the system
to skip intermediate steps. In contrast, the incorporation of
