Abstract
We carried out inelastic neutron scattering experiments on a powdered
sample of the antiferromagnetic (AFM) uniform spin-1
2 chain compound
CuSb2O6. The magnetic excitations appear in the energy range 1.8 ≤ω ≤
13 meV at 2.5 K below the AFM transition temperature (TN = 8.7 K). The
gap value (1.8 meV) is close to that evaluated from the speciﬁc heat (1.51
meV). The excitations at 12.5 K (> TN) appear gapless. Thus, the 1.8 meV
