Localization transition.–
We now use the Lanczos al-
gorithm [57, 58] to argue that the overlap of the domain
wall initial states remains finite in the thermodynamic
limit if the coupling between chains is strong enough.
To this end, we compute the Hamiltonian in the Krylov
basis {|Kn⟩} starting from an initial domain wall state
|K1⟩= |⇑· · · ⇑⇓· · · ⇓⟩(see End Matter), resulting in the
