4. POLARIZATION ANALYSIS
Utilizing the phase information successfully recovered
from the fragmented GPS-off intervals, updated polar-
ization results are calculated for the Crab pulsar using
the full reconstructed dataset. The addition of the pre-
viously phase-less 36 % of on-source events improved the
statistical precision of the phase-resolved Bayesian anal-
ysis of Stokes parameters.
Results from a Stokes analysis of the updated dataset
are shown in Figure 8 in comparison with GPS-on data
previously reported in (H. Awaki et al. 2025a).
The
polarization signal is extracted in four phase intervals:
P1, P2, bridge, and off-pulse. For the polarization anal-
ysis, the non-background-subtracted off-pulse polariza-
tion is used as the background for P1 and P2.
This
is done to isolate the polarization contribution of the
