All experiments were conducted on a system equipped with
an Intel Core i5-12400F CPU, an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060
Ti GPU, and 64 GB of DDR4 RAM.
We used gzip [20], zstd [21], and 7z [19], all configured at
their maximum compression levels (gzip -9, zstd -22, and 7z -
mx=9) as classical baselines. For neural baselines we used the
PAC [8] and TRACE [7] compressors with default parameters.
Arithmetic coding follows the configuration described in [8].
For the proposed compressor the following hyperparameters
were used: the batch size was set to |B| = 4096, and each
unit was trained for E1 = 1 epoch without information
inheritance, followed by E2 = 2 epochs with information
inheritance enabled. Optimization was performed using the
Adam optimizer with an initial learning rate of 4 × 10−3.
The learning rate was decayed by a factor of 0.8 after each
epoch. Early stopping was applied based on the validation loss,
evaluated every Kv = 1000 iterations, with patience P = 5.
The validation coefficient was fixed to ρ = 10−3. For model
weights compression, the configuration search was carried out
over b ∈{4, 8}, γ ∈{1, 2, . . . , 9} × 10−5, and V ∈{1, 2, 4}.
