is maximised at the local CFT. We have a stronger result in the more constrained case
where we have a real nonlocal family, parametrised by ∆i, that is stable to the nonlocal
deformations in the IR. That is, if all of the nonlocal operators become irrelevant in the IR
near the local CFT, then the Hessian at the local point, ∂∆i∂∆j ˜F|SR, is negative definite –
and so ˜F({∆i}) is at a multidimensional local maximum.
