– 5 –
2.2
The result should not be surprising
This observation of F-extremisation should not be surprising. We have taken a local CFT,
generalised it to a line of nonlocal CFTs, and asked how the original CFT is special. An
extremisation principle is natural, and the free energy is the most natural single number
used to measure a CFT. The fact that we find a simpler representation of the scaling
dimension of the fundamental fields is a little surprising, and very neat.
