3.3
A duality at fixed points
It is not immediately obvious that these two routes end up defining the same CFT. Indeed,
they are not the same quantum field theories away from the fixed point; it is now well
established that generically they will lie in the same universality class, in that they will
flow to the same IR CFT. This was the argument of [1, 63]; note, however that a full proof
has not yet been provided.
