In fact, both mixed neighborhood diversity and mixed cliquewidth bound their transitive
closure counterparts, as shown in the following.
▶Proposition 12 (⋆). For any mixed graph G (without directed cycles), mnd+(G) ⩽mnd(G)
and mcw+(G) ⩽4mcw(G) · mcw(G).
Idea. For mixed neighborhood diversity, it holds that two vertices u, v of the same type in G
