dealer of each team can hold a token for every team, i.e., 𝑑(𝑡1,𝑡2) indicates that the dealer of 𝑡1 still
holds the token associated with 𝑡2. The players are no longer part of the modeled protocol.
Initially there is at least one inactive team, and dealers hold all tokens:
