When the body is immersed in the weak tidal field of a distant companion, spherical symmetry is broken, and the
potential admits a multipolar expansion. In the static or adiabatic regime, in which the external field changes on a
timescale much longer than the body’s internal dynamical time, one may write
U = −GM
