2. Toric ALE and ALF gravitational instantons
2.1. Einstein equations and rod structure. We begin by introducing the basic definitions and
properties of toric instantons, as discussed in more detail in [19]. We then introduce the asymptotic
types that we will consider.
Definition 2.1. A toric gravitational instanton is a complete, simply connected, Riemannian man-
ifold (M, g) that is Ricci flat, which admits an (effective) isometric torus T action with at least one
fixed point. We assume this action has no points with discrete isotropy subgroups.
It has been shown that under these assumptions the orbit space ˆ
