We first introduce the asymptotics of interest in a general setting.
Definition 2.2. A Riemannian manifold (M, g) is ALE of order τ > 0 if [3]:
• It has an end diffeomorphic to R × S where S = S3/Γ and Γ is a finite subgroup of O(4).
• S admits a Riemannian metric γ is constant curvature +1.
• On the end
(2.4)
