Killing fields. Therefore, for large enough ρ0 > 0, the curve ρ = ρ0 is in the asymptotic end, which
implies the region ρ > ρ0 is simply connected. But since ˆ
M is simply connected, this implies the
complement 0 < ρ < ρ0 is also simply connected. Hence, by the uniformisation theorem we can
conformally map the region 0 < ρ < ρ0 to the strip 0 < Im w < ρ0 in the complex w-plane such
that ρ = 0 corresponds to Re w = 0 and ρ = ρ0 to Im w = ρ0. Therefore, ρ −Im w is harmonic
in this strip of the w-plane and vanishes at its boundaries, so by the maximum principle ρ = Im w.
Therefore, w = z + iρ is a global holomorphic coordinate on the orbit space.
□
