Remark: We note that the existing analysis of JFFS in [5] only modeled the system state by a scalar
𝑍(𝑡) := Í𝐾
𝑙=0 𝑍𝑙(𝑡) (i.e., the total number of jobs in the system at time 𝑡), under the assumption that jobs will
