4.2
PETALS-based Experiments
4.2.1
Experiment Settings
We modify PETALS [6] to implement the proposed server chain composition and load balancing algo-
rithms12. We deploy the system onto a server with 3 A100 (80 GB) GPUs, where we leverage the multi-
instance GPU technology [8] to partition each A100 into 2 lower-performance GPUs (2g.20gb) and 1
higher-performance GPU (3g.40gb) that together emulate 9 servers with one GPU each. Due to the limited
GPUs, we use a smaller model LLaMA-2-7B for the experiment. We use the namespace and the traffic
control features of Linux [27] to simulate network latency according to the RTTs in RIPE Atlas European
network [25] as described in Section 4.1.1. We generate requests according to the Azure LLM inference
trace from [24], which contains the arrival times and the numbers of input/output tokens from sampled
LLM inference services in Azure, collected on November 11th 2023. The trace has an average rate of 2.57
requests/s, an average input length of 2048 tokens, and an average output length of 28 tokens.
