where γ is a dimensionless deformation parameter. At the classical level, the T ¯T and root-T ¯T
flows commute, and the latter admits a geometric realization as a non-linear transformation of
the dynamical variables [35]. At the quantum level, however, the structure of the deformation
is much less understood. Existing work has mainly focused on the definition of the operator [37]
and on its gravitational formulation [38], while a systematic analysis of local correlators is still
lacking [37]. From the field-theoretic viewpoint, the root-T ¯T operator is non-analytic and
therefore does not fit directly into the standard perturbative framework developed for T ¯T
deformations.
In this paper, quasi-primary correlators in a two-dimensional CFT deformed simultane-
ously by T ¯T and root-T ¯T are studied within the random-geometry framework of [33]. An
effective geometric description of the combined flow is first constructed using a convenient
parametrization of the frame field. In this framework, the deformed two-point function is
obtained to all orders in the T ¯T coupling and to leading order in the root-T ¯T coupling.
The leading correction to the three-point function under the combined deformation is then
computed. Finally, the contributions of both T ¯T and root-T ¯T are shown to admit a reinter-
pretation as a weighted average of undeformed CFT correlators over conformal dimensions.
The paper is organized as follows. Sec. 2 sets up the path integral formulation for the
combined T ¯T and root-T ¯T deformation.
Sec. 3 contains the perturbative computation of
– 3 –
the two-point function to leading order in the root-T ¯T coupling and to all orders in T ¯T, and
presents the kernels that express the deformed correlators as weighted averages over conformal
dimensions.
Sec. 4 gives the leading perturbative correction to the three-point correlator.
Conclusions and an outlook are provided in Sec. 5. Technical details are relegated to the
appendices.
