norm (see [33] for derivation and proofs of relevant bounds).
We start by defining the grid and scalar function space over it.
grid = Grid(30, 30)
U = FunctionSpace(grid)
To apply the Dirichlet boundary conditions on the entire boundary, we first
define a function that selects all the boundary points.
def U_mask_fun(i, j):
edges_x = (0, grid.n[0])
edges_y = (0, grid.n[1])
m = 0 if i in edges_x or j in edges_y else 1
return m
We can use it to select the corresponding degrees of freedom from the U space.
u_mask = GridFunction(U_mask_fun, grid)
U_bc = select_dofs(U, u_mask, invert=True)
The definition of the bilinear form and assembling its matrix is now simple.
def B_form(u, v):
return dot(grad(u, ""+""), grad(v, ""+""))
