solution exhibits some distortions and asymmetry, the results obtained on the
40 × 40 grid are close to the exact analytical solution given above. The loss and
true error throughout the training process are presented in fig. 5. It clearly shows
that the error does stay within the bounds predicted by the theoretical analysis
carried out in section 3. In fact, the error is rather close to the lower bound. This
can be explained by the fact that the upper bound is controlled by the smallest
