2604.14911v1,Landau damping on expanding backgrounds,"We analyse the effect of expansion in Newtonian cosmology on the asymptotic behaviour of charged self-interacting plasmas close to Poisson equilibria. To this end, we study the Vlasov-Poisson system on the phase space of a $3$-torus which is expanding with respect to the scale factor $a(t)$. We show that, for $a(t)=t^q$ with $q\in(0,\frac12)$, solutions to this system exhibit nonlinear Landau damping for initial data that is small with respect to a suitably strong Gevrey class, i.e., the charge density contrast of the plasma decays superpolynomially. For larger choices of $q$ within this range, the initial data requirements become stricter while the decay weakens. To our knowledge, this is the first result showing Landau damping in a cosmological setting.","['David Fajman', 'Liam Urban']",2026-04-16,0,https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.14911v1,math.AP,"LANDAU DAMPING ON EXPANDING BACKGROUNDS
DAVID FAJMAN, LIAM URBAN
Abstract
We analyse the effect of expansion in Newtonian cosmology on the asymptotic behaviour of charged
self-interacting plasmas close to Poisson equilibria. To this end, we study the Vlasov-Poisson system on
the phase space of a 3-torus which is expanding with respect to the scale factor a(t). We show that, for
a(t) = tq with q ∈(0, 1
2), solutions to this system exhibit nonlinear Landau damping for initial data that is
small with respect to a suitably strong Gevrey class, i.e., the charge density contrast of the plasma decays
superpolynomially. For larger choices of q within this range, the initial data requirements become stricter
while the decay weakens. To our knowledge, this is the first result showing Landau damping in a cosmological
setting.
1. Introduction
