2. Preliminaries, main theorem and proof overview
In this section, after setting up notation and showing that the system (1.2) is locally well-
posed at the level of Gevrey regularity, we renormalise (1.2) to, in particular, derive the family of
Volterra equations (2.11a) for non-zero modes of the rescaled density, which form the centerpiece
of our damping analysis. We do all of this first for a general positive analytic background µ before
restricting to the Poisson background when introducing Theorem 2.8 and discussing its proof.
